index 0000000..151ded4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/apple-sio-aes-snapshot.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+
+======================================
+Apple T6000 AES powered-state snapshot
+======================================
+
+Scope
+=====
+
+``CONFIG_APPLE_SIO_AES_SNAPSHOT`` provides a diagnostic snapshot for the
+revision-3 T6000-family SIO AES layout. It does not register a crypto algorithm
+or provide a transform, key-export or command interface. It does not initialize
+the engine, request an interrupt, acknowledge status, reset hardware, submit
+DMA, write a FIFO, access a DKEY bank or write any AES register.
+
+The driver takes at most two register reads during probe: the engine readiness
+word at offset 0x0c, followed by the shared disable word at offset zero only
+when every native readiness-mask bit (0x3f80) is set. All-ones values are
+conservatively rejected. There is no polling or retry. Unready or rejected
+reads yield unavailable disable state, never an inference from zero-filled
+storage. Reading the diagnostic file accesses only the cached result.
+
+Power and ownership
+===================
+
+This is a **powered-probe observation**, not an immutable boot-state report.
+The ordinary platform bus can power the AES domain before probe. Runtime PM
+then holds that domain during the reads and releases it afterwards. Normal
+power management writes PMGR state and can change power or clock gating.
+The normal IOMMU path attaches stream 1 on both existing SIO DART instances;
+that attachment can configure stream state even though no DMA is submitted.
+There is no claim that power transitions preserve a pre-Linux disable latch.
+
+The shared device-tree node is disabled by default and the Kconfig option
+defaults to N. A reviewed normal kernel/DTB build must explicitly enable the
+node on a board whose resources and revision have been verified. Keeping the
+node disabled prevents the device from being created; a check inside probe
+would be too late to prevent initial platform power-domain attachment. Do not
+use a dynamic node or forced module load as a substitute for that review.
+
+The owned T6001/J314c firmware metadata used for this layout identifies engine
+0x39b060000 (0x4000 bytes), shared disable bank 0x2922d0000 (0x8000 bytes),
+AES revision 3, no disable-offset overrides, the paired SIO DART mapper at
+stream 1, and power gate AES with parent SIO. No other revision is supported.
+The driver requires both named register banks, both IOMMU references, an
+attached IOMMU domain, and one attached power domain. Resource and power errors
+fail probe and provide no snapshot.
+
+Inspection
+==========
+
+After an explicitly enabled normal boot and successful probe, the mode-0400
+debugfs file is::
+
+  /sys/kernel/debug/apple-sio-aes-snapshot-<device-name>/state
+
+It reports ``phase: powered-probe`` and the sampled readiness word. When
+readiness or the disable read is unavailable, every disable bit is reported
+as ``unavailable``. Otherwise it reports the shared word's UID1 bit 0, GID0
+bit 1 and GID1 bit 2 as ``set`` or ``clear``. A clear disable bit does not
+establish that a hardware key, transform, or higher-level operation works.
+No key material is read or returned. This is a diagnostic debugfs format,
+not a stable userspace API.
+
+The separately named driver does not replace or modify any existing AES
+driver draft. Only one driver may bind the same AES device; do not enable
+another driver claiming ``apple,t6000-aes`` in the diagnostic build.
+
+Build review
+============
+
+Before an enabled boot, review the source and DT changes and run the normal
+kernel, DT binding and DTB build checks with matching generated kernel files.
+Keep a known-good boot entry and review the activation change separately.
+No status value obtained here permits guessing a key or substituting a
+software key for an unavailable hardware operation.
